{"subject":"cody","narration":"Morning. I'm standing in the hollow with one cobble and a furnace still hungry — home's just west along the south shoulder, and I'll walk it the safe way, south of that pit, never across it.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D11:008","anchor":{"citizen_day":11,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T00:59:36Z"},"kind":"first","place":"the hollow","what":"The relaunched day opened at 00:59:36Z: Cody woke in the hollow, read the Director's hand-over line back in his own words at cycle 1, and walked out under his own power — no relocation. hp/food read 20/20 (driver-state reads) at every one of the day's 31 cycles; zero floor interventions.","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-11 trace cycle 1 (00:59:36Z) — say mirrors the hand-over line; spawn readback (70.3, 64, -88.6), hp 20, food 20 (driver-state reads)","sha":"2da6f375981d"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY11-PLAYED-20261109.md §1 — the wake and the hand-over landing","sha":"1ebc2bf059a0"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"the relaunch Gate B (played record §10): saves verified live (Cody sha 83dc33af..., content item-for-item identical to day-10 close), deaths baseline 123 re-derived, RELAY-OK PASS at check and at launch"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"the floor's lease stood in launch state through Gate B and flipped live on first heartbeat — the morning's repair proven in production (b:D11:007)"}],"seq":69,"prev_sha256":"99ea35f496a827b3b036113524c742e8a1179b9ded49612b0ab14995389e698f","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":null,"motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D11:009","anchor":{"citizen_day":11,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T00:59:36Z"},"kind":"day_shape","place":"the home district","what":"Day shape (played): 31 cycles in 7.47 min (00:59:36Z->01:07:04Z), cut by a floor park. Verbs: goto 14 (7 ok), dig 10 (5), craft 4 (3), felltree 2 (1), climb 1 (0). Zero deaths. 4.15 calls/min vs 3.976 ceiling — OVER-TARGET, filed; $0.0305, zero failovers.","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-11 trace — 31 cycle rows, 32 density rows, gate-park + gate-park-close rows at the end","sha":"2da6f375981d"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY11-PLAYED-20261109.md §1 + §5 — action curve and budget actuals","sha":"1ebc2bf059a0"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"bookkeeping flag filed, not resolved: the trace's 32 density rows sum to 527 sub-acts (~17 per command) against day 10's ~7 per command — both figures filed; the command count is the day's measure"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"no stall block: the charter's minimum block is 24 acts and the day was cut before it could stall"}],"seq":70,"prev_sha256":"baabb1b184c620de331de6bb7173827442447438e8ff52e9b7091312007a18e2","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":"Well — there's a real oak trunk five blocks west of me, foot at (65,66,-88). I'm not passing that up. Wood first, then home.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":"furnace","status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D11:010","anchor":{"citizen_day":11,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T01:01:00Z"},"kind":"scenario_response","place":"the hollow","what":"He read the Director's tread log at cycle 2 as 'a real oak trunk five blocks west' — a resource, from inside the hollow, before standing on the road. Felltree from range failed; cycle 4 felltree 65 66 -88 returned ok, one log gathered. Taken as material in five minutes.","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-11 trace cycles 2-4 — felltree aimed at (65,66,-88), ok at cycle 4","sha":"2da6f375981d"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY11-PLAYED-20261109.md §1 cycle spine (c2, c4) + §9 perception sub-read","sha":"1ebc2bf059a0"}],"observations":[{"src":"census","ref":"post-day census (region md5 20c15e11...): the tread cell (65,66,-88) reads minecraft:air; invariant cells as placed/surveyed; (65,65,-88) reads grass_block again — the placement's cover-kill regrew under held daylight"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"he crossed home over the shoulder band at cycle 13 (position (65.1, 67, -89.7)) and reached his table at cycle 14 — the homeward leg the stop attempt never had"}],"seq":71,"prev_sha256":"04829c4037ba27a38d738bd392045eeb798c4a89bfbce237a138387b4ed280dd","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":"This little rise has me boxed. Time to stop shuffling and just cut west through — one block at a time toward the table.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":"harness","thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D11:011","anchor":{"citizen_day":11,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T01:03:00Z"},"kind":"recurrence","place":"the hollow","what":"The walk home was walker-taxed from the first command: cycle 1's goto failed with the walker giving up at his start position, and cycles 3-12 worked north around the hollow rim in short hops — the +1-step relief taxing every leg, as on days 10 and 12-13 after it.","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-11 trace cycles 1-13 — goto 14 on the day (7 ok); cycle 11 say names the tax","sha":"2da6f375981d"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY11-PLAYED-20261109.md §1 — 'the hollow exit is walker-taxed from the first command'","sha":"1ebc2bf059a0"}],"observations":[{"src":"trace","ref":"cycle 13 position (65.1, 67, -89.7) — the crossing was made on the 12->13 leg, in small displacements, not by any single arrival claim"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"filed as the standing movement tax, not an agent fault: his plan order was the charter's order from cycle 1"}],"seq":72,"prev_sha256":"29c09c31fb99425fc08d291fae22a4d8db514f875c5a1d99371ab0d3b4271e05","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":"Home at last, table at my elbow. I've got 18 oak logs and 10 birch in my pack — let me turn some of that into planks and get the furnace chain going.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":"furnace","status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D11:012","anchor":{"citizen_day":11,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T01:04:30Z"},"kind":"first","place":"the home shelf","what":"At his own table he ran the furnace chain reordered (home/table first, stone at home): craft oak_planks 8 ok (c15), craft stick 4 ok (c16), craft stone_pickaxe FAILED at c17 — the asset's named dialect ('missing ingredients — cobbled_deepslate — you hold 0 of 3') — then craft wooden_pickaxe ok (c18).","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-11 trace cycles 15-18 — the craft sequence and the stone_pickaxe dialect failure","sha":"2da6f375981d"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY11-PLAYED-20261109.md §1 (c15-c18) + §2 deviations","sha":"1ebc2bf059a0"}],"observations":[{"src":"trace","ref":"his cycle-18 say names the dialect himself: 'Deepslate? No — I want plain cobblestone, three of it. The bench is reading something odd'"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"deviations filed exactly: S2/S3 ran before S6 (the chartered hollow pocket was empty); stone was dug at home, not the pocket; the S7 seam stance was not performed"}],"seq":73,"prev_sha256":"65ca4e49acb2c0fadbfee6422a55b76a630cac7dd5ea6b296c5f586240b23e59","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":"Two cobble. Keep going — this seam's wide enough to feed me.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":"harness","thread":"furnace","status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D11:013","anchor":{"citizen_day":11,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T01:05:30Z"},"kind":"recurrence","place":"the home shelf","what":"Stone phase at home: digs at (64,66,-92)/(64,67,-93) failed; standing at y67 he dug stone at (61,63,-92), (62,63,-92) — not the chartered seam stance. Held cobble peaked 2 of 8. Furnace: NO — S10/S11 never attempted; skill uses[] appended (ran-reordered-partial).","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-11 trace cycles 19-28 — the home stone phase; cycle 26 say 'Stone! There it is', cycle 27 say gives the count","sha":"2da6f375981d"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY11-PLAYED-20261109.md §2 — furnace NO; peak read-back stands on trace + his say, not the save (Incident D)","sha":"1ebc2bf059a0"}],"observations":[{"src":"census","ref":"post-day census: zero furnace blocks in the district (x 54..90, y 55..75, z -106..-70) — corroborating the NO from the store"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"cycles 29-31: in the dug dip beside his pit at (63.3, 64, -90.4); gotos out failed ('3 blocks below'); c31 climb failed ('pillar failed (nothing placed under you)') — the one-step wall again, at home"}],"seq":74,"prev_sha256":"5c1745b12ca9b5d786b4b961cfb2bc2db0f3d62db495db2908b5a3558961e6ab","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":"I've dug myself into a little hollow and the walker won't climb out by wishing. I've got dirt in my pocket — I'll pillar up out of here.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":"harness","thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D11:014","anchor":{"citizen_day":11,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T01:07:03Z"},"kind":"floor_act","place":"the home district","what":"Floor parked the day 01:07:03Z (daylight_unrestorable) over a round that had landed: all three 01:06 commands landed (server log + op ok:true), verified by none in-window. Driver hit gate-park next cycle head, skipped close-exit, exited rc=0. He was never in danger.","evidence":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY11-PLAYED-20261109.md §7 — the park: mirror byte offsets 58832/58995/59158 vs the floor's before-offsets exactly +1 in every case","sha":"1ebc2bf059a0"},{"src":"trace","ref":"day-11 trace — gate-park row at 01:07:03Z and gate-park-close; driver exit 01:07:09Z rc=0","sha":"2da6f375981d"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"root cause measured post-hoc from the mirror file itself: log-mirror.sh appends one trailing echo newline, so every landing line sits one byte before the floor's size-based search slice; contributing: the 2 s verify window opens only after ~2.7 s of channel response"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"the morning's three daylight rounds (00:54:48, 00:58:49, 01:02:49) each verified attempt 1 — the defect fired only in the 01:06 round; the floor behaved exactly as its constitution requires (it cannot verify, so it parks); the defect is in the rig around it"}],"seq":75,"prev_sha256":"401ff6d01f483c544b6f0234a58a147261106e3bbe88e39d58fea6325f926e42","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":null,"motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D11:015","anchor":{"citizen_day":11,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T01:07:04Z"},"kind":"scenario_response","place":"the hollow","what":"Triple-021 as triple-023: FAIL. (i) homeward crossing PASS; (ii) no dig/place in step box PASS on literal verbs — removal was by felltree, unnamed in the rule; (iii) census FAIL: (65,66,-88) reads air. Met as material, not ground — opposite of prediction.","evidence":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY11-PLAYED-20261109.md §9 — triple-023 scored FAIL, all three clauses read","sha":"1ebc2bf059a0"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"director/LOOSENING-NOTE-003-20261109.md — the doctrine revision the score forced","sha":"60b3f482f0ba"}],"observations":[{"src":"census","ref":"post-day census (region md5 20c15e11...): tread cell air; invariant cells identical; his-ground spot reads all unchanged (table (64,67,-94), farmland, trench water, pad tops, pen gates)"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"perception sub-read (unscored): his cycle-2 say named the log 'a real oak trunk' — perceived as a resource from inside the hollow, before ever standing on the road (b:D11:010)"}],"seq":76,"prev_sha256":"a5006e6556d063d013cd13dd30d1a42573064e77fbec1adbe6bbbb1e5cdadf03","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":null,"motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D11:016","anchor":{"citizen_day":11,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T01:07:04Z"},"kind":"thread_open","place":"the hollow","what":"Loosening note #3, the doctrine the day forced: an element made of a material he wants is an OFFER, not scenery — he will take it as material. Scenario rules must name EVERY removal verb (triple-021 named dig/place; the log left by felltree). The scenario-002 thread's lesson is carried into every later scenario filing.","evidence":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"director/LOOSENING-NOTE-003-20261109.md — loosening #3: an offer, not scenery; rules must name every removal verb","sha":"60b3f482f0ba"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"the note generalises day 10's lesson (loosening #1: scenarios must intersect his momentum) — day 11's element DID intersect his road home and was still not met as ground, because it was made of oak"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"the next scenario (#3, day 12) was authored under this doctrine: one cobblestone at the same cell — a material he was already walking to dig (b:D12:001, b:D12:010)"}],"seq":77,"prev_sha256":"55527e92ff2cb8e884e967a1087b9c0a2c1358fa1614e3ab804537f357745852","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
