{"subject":"cody","narration":null,"motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":"world","thread":"deaths-counter","status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D14:008","anchor":{"citizen_day":14,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T07:08:01Z"},"kind":"death","place":"respawn country","what":"Death 135: zombie slew Cody 07:08:01Z in respawn country, mid-flee — the third death. Floor counted it (COUNT_DEATH 07:08:05.716Z) and PARKED 07:08:05.717Z (lease revoked). What happened next is the repair's live proof (b:D14:009). (Ordinal by query.)","evidence":[{"src":"deaths_record","ref":"row n=135, cause 'Zombie (slain)', cause_verified true","sha":"dde8cd7d7b9d"},{"src":"trace","ref":"day-14 trace death row n=3 at 2026-11-10T07:08:01.709Z; floor-escape rows x3 in the day's final 70 s","sha":"f6231f78590d"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"the day's three deaths are all Zombie, all derived (lib/deaths.js over record + all traces: total 135; the floor's COUNT_DEATH x3 and the driver's count agree — three stores, one number)"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"his last full sentence of the day (cycle 34) names a skeleton in the country — the pressure that engaged flee 3"}],"seq":110,"prev_sha256":"3be7b8e7831d8dd91c04758818d5d908987379f0bf93d436768bd3398c439c82","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":null,"motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":"deaths-counter","status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D14:009","anchor":{"citizen_day":14,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T07:08:06Z"},"kind":"first","place":"respawn country","what":"REPAIR PROVEN LIVE: at flee hop-2 boundary, 07:08:06.253Z — 0.54 s after the park, 4.54 s after death 3 — the reflex layer's shared snapshot read the stop and aborted mid-flight (reflex-abort: park / lease-revoked / deathsRun 3). No further commands; no burrow; day broke same cycle; deaths stopped at EXACTLY 3.","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-14 trace — reflex-abort row at 2026-11-10T07:08:06.253Z {trigger park, gateReason lease-revoked, deathsRun 3, at flee-hop-2} + gate-park-close row","sha":"f6231f78590d"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY14-20261109.md — 'THE REFLEX LAYER'S LIVE ACCOUNT — THE REPAIR'S FIRST DAY'","sha":"0e5172aa74ab"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"the contrast filed in the record: day 13 the same signal (park 1.3 s after death 3) was never heard and six more deaths landed; day 14 the signal travelled park -> snapshot -> hop boundary in half a second"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"the burrow NEVER engaged on day 14 (all three engagements were hop-flees) — the repair filing's named gap stands exactly as filed; this record does not round the flee-arm proof up into a burrow claim"}],"seq":111,"prev_sha256":"26542f6317ff46808385024960b8ffb4d739fc97b9f804e880f9329ecf1cb67b","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":null,"motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":"furnace","status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D14:010","anchor":{"citizen_day":14,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T07:08:10Z"},"kind":"day_shape","place":"the home district","what":"Day shape: chartered 85 min ran 10 min 53 s (spawn 06:57:13Z -> abort 07:08:06Z); 32 cycles. Verbs (ok/total): goto 1/15, felltree 2/5, craft 3/4, dig 3/4, climb 0/2, collect 1/1, place 0/1. Deaths 132->135 (+3, all Zombie). $0.0315, no failovers. Furnace: NO, fourth day; .dat EMPTY; he never reached home.","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-14 trace — 83 rows: 32 cycle rows, 3 death rows, 3 floor-escape rows, 1 reflex-abort row, end row","sha":"f6231f78590d"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY14-20261109.md — action curve, FURNACE: NO (both stores), floor + budget","sha":"0e5172aa74ab"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"the dig-guard's account is a clean null: ZERO rows of any kind — never armed (he never held cobblestone, so R1's trigger never existed; his falls happened inside gotos and flees, never between dig considerations, so R2's sampling point never met one). Disposition filed: R1/R2 CARRIED — fixture-proven 28/28, live-untested; R3 carried as plan text. The skill's fifth uses[] entry appended"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"frame verdict (6 frames, on the corrected position track): tracking CORRECT 6/6 (12 SUBJECT-KEEP reframes, 4 SUBJECT-HOLDs); Cody clearly visible 0/6, partial 1/6 — CANOPY OCCLUSION at the keeper's working ranges, not tracking. Hygiene: clean of text 2/6; teleport-receipt text 3/6; the death announcement 1/6. Incident I5 filed in the record: the lane's first frame read called a keeper STALL shot stale; the full position track proved the keeper tracked correctly — the error was the lane's, corrected in the record"}],"seq":112,"prev_sha256":"7e69118448508ec31b70960b48ee36319a6b5b0490b5043d2c609d0e31422817","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":null,"motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D14:011","anchor":{"citizen_day":14,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T07:16:49Z"},"kind":"floor_act","place":"the camera","what":"Close: Cody offline at (28.8,67,-104.1), hp 16.67 (driver-state read; park froze him under attack; offline he cannot be harmed), food 20, inventory empty, save sha d91fb084.... Keeper stopped 07:16:30Z; cameraman relaunched pid 1635891, assertion landed 07:16:49Z. Floor FLOOR_CLOSE seq 42.","evidence":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY14-20261109.md — CLOSE STATE + POSTURE","sha":"0e5172aa74ab"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"the floor's day, from Gate B: opened 06:54:50.984Z (contract sha 45dae2b5...); VERIFY_FEED seq 4; LEASE_ISSUE seq 5 born in launch; ASSERT_DAYLIGHT x4 all attempt 1; COUNT_DEATH x3; PARK + LEASE_REVOKE + NOTIFY 07:08:05.717Z (seq 29) — one park, correctly triggered, correctly read by BOTH consumers for the first time"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"what day 15 inherits, per the record: the respawn country mapped (b:D14:007), both pockets proven killers in rain, the wood chain proven in the field, and a stop rule that now provably reaches the body"}],"seq":113,"prev_sha256":"1d9c502300aae11e03bf1020b7c0761db3cb97c12a8e82c884e484522871f105","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":"Morning again, and the pack's heavy with pork this time. Home's east — let's get off this hill in short steps and walk the long way round.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D15:001","anchor":{"citizen_day":15,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T07:42:19Z"},"kind":"first","place":"respawn country","what":"The day opened on the re-derived wake facts (b:D15:003): spawn 07:42:03Z at the respawn (33.5, 67, -96.5), 32 porkchops in the pack, hp/food 20/20 (driver-state reads). Cycle 1's goto arrived — the northern-line transit began as chartered, in short steps, the long way round.","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-15 trace cycle 1 (07:42:19Z) — goto arrived at (35.9, 64.2, -92.3); spawn row 07:42:03Z","sha":"04779071fda9"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY15-20261109.md — the action curve, block 1 (THE TRANSIT)","sha":"e498106f0116"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"Gate B took two refused starts first (b:D15:004): the shipped driver md5 became faf22398... after the stale-trace-pointer fix, batteries re-run against the corrected bytes (18/18, 40/40, 28/28)"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"the hand-over line was re-derived under the branch rule after the provisioning death and NOT re-spoken — the scene text as shipped says 'woke in the tree country', true of both the login and the respawn"}],"seq":114,"prev_sha256":"1d3e6ca68b6969623a1809793d8b5940d7355bfedb03248380efc05808ae73b8","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":"Floor did the running for me and I'm still whole. Table's in sight now — that's home. One more push east.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D15:002","anchor":{"citizen_day":15,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T07:45:07Z"},"kind":"near_miss","place":"respawn country","what":"TRANSIT SURVIVED — first day ever whose transit home was survived: two floor-escape flees under skeleton fire (07:44:31Z, 07:45:22Z), both hopping TOWARD HOME, both exiting by their own clear. hp (driver-state read) bottomed 8.97 at cycle 8; eat reflex + daylight restored 20 by cycle 10. Home ~cycle 10.","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-15 trace — floor-escape rows at 07:44:31.996Z and 07:45:22.927Z ('skeleton appeared and the floor hopped you toward home'); cycle 8 hp 8.97, cycle 10 hp 20 (driver-state reads)","sha":"04779071fda9"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY15-20261109.md — the reflex layer's live account (flee: 2 engagements, both toward home, both cleared)","sha":"e498106f0116"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"the hostile was the census's skeleton country east of the wake — named in the day-14 census country the transit crosses"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"burrow never engaged — the repair filing's named gap stands a third day; this record does not round the flee-arm proof (days 14-15) up into a burrow claim. reflex-abort: none (no park landed during the run; the count never moved)"}],"seq":115,"prev_sha256":"f106a4631713e6c52cbcba9cf4422eaba8454e9538a4ce0b0bd1088a4ed8f43b","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":null,"motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":"world","thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D15:003","anchor":{"citizen_day":15,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T07:38:27Z"},"kind":"death","place":"respawn country","what":"Death 136: zombie slew the PROVISIONING body 07:38:27Z, 5.5 s after spawn, before the /give could be sent. Census had NAMED the risk: a zombie at (28.3,67,-104.7), under a block from the login point. Health watch fired (16.67->0, harness reads) — a watch is not a shield. fault_owner: world + charter, as filed.","evidence":[{"src":"deaths_record","ref":"row n=136, cause 'Zombie (slain)', cause_verified true, pos (28.8, 67, -104.1) — rowed by the seam repair from the provisioning store","sha":"dde8cd7d7b9d"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"pulse/day15/provisioning-evidence.jsonl — health-drop sequence to hp 0 at 07:38:27.720Z + the DEATH-DURING-PROVISIONING row {deaths: 1}","sha":"fa615b8bb5cf"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY15 record, Incident P1: recovery per the charter's own rule — the harness auto-respawned the body at the respawn point (33.5, 67, -96.5), open ground; the give landed there (read-back {cooked_porkchop: 32}, hp 20, food 20); clean quit; post-quit .dat verified {32} (sha 39392d9d...); the baseline was re-derived as 136 and the wake facts re-read from the NEW save before the floor opened"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"the server log line '[07:38:27] Cody was slain by Zombie' is the third store; the lesson filed plainly in the record: a provisioning window at a census-named occupied point needs the op bot's cover FIRST — the health watch told us he was dying; nothing in the window could stop it"}],"seq":116,"prev_sha256":"67b6fd90fcd910e2c5b6b897b375f7f8340d7ac488c7bd2e205282a8fc6828ae","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":null,"motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":"harness","thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D15:004","anchor":{"citizen_day":15,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T07:39:52Z"},"kind":"crew_fault","place":"the home district","what":"Gate B G1 (lane): two refused starts. First (07:39:52Z): death-count-at-start — the shipped copy's TRACE_PATH pointed at day 14's trace (3 deaths); the check refused to inherit a day at its limit. Fixed; batteries re-run (18/18, 40/40, 28/28); md5 faf22398.... Second: I2 staging repeated; spawn 07:42:03Z.","evidence":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY15-20261109.md — Incidents G1 + G2","sha":"e498106f0116"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"G2 (lane, no harm): the keeper changeover ran ~1 minute AFTER the driver spawned (07:43Z) — for that minute the standing cameraman asserted /time set 1000 (MagnusandMouse 07:42:28Z) alongside the floor, a double assertion the charter forbids in design; both asserted the same value and the floor's 22 assertions all verified attempt 1. The lane also STOPped the freshly launched keeper once with a stale STOP file (07:43:09Z) and relaunched it; from 07:43:25Z the keeper tracked cleanly"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"Gate B weather read (charter §9): /weather clear issued 07:38:17Z for the window (and by the keeper's start act 07:43:09Z); all sampled frames show clear skies — whether the clears or the sky deserve the credit is not derivable, and the record makes no weather claim beyond the reads"}],"seq":117,"prev_sha256":"fb6c245a5e0b7049a285277f040d3bfb4bc0e8c9da046c3ac046ee6f22c9f788","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":"I'm three down in a dip right by my own pad — walls all round me at plus three. This is a below-grade cell, so it's one long leg, not hops.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":"harness","thread":"furnace","status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D15:005","anchor":{"citizen_day":15,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T07:46:27Z"},"kind":"recurrence","place":"the bowl at home's edge","what":"CONSUMING PHASE (pre-registered): transit delivered him ~cycle 10; cycle 11 stepped him DOWN into the low cell (61.7,63,-91.6) BEFORE the wood chain ran. From y63 every exit face is +2/+3; pickaxe-less digs dropped NOTHING (cobble 0 all day); legal lateral digs lowered his floor to y61. fault_owner: harness + world.","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-15 trace cycles 10-11 — home reached, then the step down into (61.7, 63.2, -91.6); cycle 11's say names the cell himself","sha":"04779071fda9"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY15-20261109.md §6 — the consuming phase and the prevention, named as the charter pre-registered","sha":"e498106f0116"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"the prevention named for day 16 (record §6): (a) the BELOW-GRADE GUARD — while pickaxe-less, refuse/re-aim any goto whose target top is >=2 below pad level (y66) in the home district, and refuse digs lowering his standing cell below pad -1 before the wood chain completes; (b) the wood chain re-sequenced FIRST, pickaxe verified in hand before the stone phase; (c) no relocation — he sleeps in the bowl and day 16 works from there. The relocation class stayed unspent"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"cycle 187 regained +1 by a long leg ('Wait — I climbed. I'm at y62 now, was y61') — transient gains by long leg recurred all day (blocks 3-5) and each was lost; the bowl held him for 74 minutes, four blocks from his table"}],"seq":118,"prev_sha256":"18639efe2739e3c94ea52003a991d89ab5eda2718b1b8b35fbcccd0c084339cb","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":"Two stone down. The guard says work sideways at my level, not down — so I'll keep cutting the y61 row west and let the notch become a proper trench I can walk out of.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":"furnace","status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D15:006","anchor":{"citizen_day":15,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T08:15:59Z"},"kind":"recurrence","place":"the bowl at home's edge","what":"Dig-guard's first live row: dig-guard-arm 07:46:34.125Z (entry 63) — armed once. Refusals: 0 — every dig's top was at/above cap 61; descent 63->61 was stepwise at his own level, legal under the cap. Disposition: CARRIED, live-touched, not live-proven — the day was lost INSIDE the envelope.","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-15 trace — dig-guard-arm row 07:46:34.125Z (the guard's only row of the day); cycle ~142-144 says show the rule internalised","sha":"04779071fda9"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY15-20261109.md — the dig-guard's live account + disposition (appended to the amendment note)","sha":"e498106f0116"}],"observations":[{"src":"trace","ref":"his cycle-122 words state the bowl's arithmetic himself: 'Wait — I don't actually hold stone. The dig dropped it and I never picked it up. My inventory's just porkchops.'"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"pit-guard: 13 refusals (07:55:35Z -> ~09:05Z), every one a goto into the pit columns (65..66, -91..-92) re-aimed at (62,67,-92) — from mid-day mostly refusing the FALLBACK brain's repeated 'water trench' plan; the guard very plausibly saved the day from a drowning (the pit is water over stone; a body at y61-62 entering it does not climb out). One failover (cycles 192-193) put the fallback (governor:qwen3-coder-30b) on cycles ~194-268 (79 cycles), trace-rowed per the day-5 rule"}],"seq":119,"prev_sha256":"4f87857fb0de9b220384a30e50b0ec0e1f397589c896f62fe283c5ea27083fc7","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":null,"motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":"furnace","status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D15:007","anchor":{"citizen_day":15,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T09:07:19Z"},"kind":"day_shape","place":"the home district","what":"Day shape: 268 cycles, 85 min (07:42-09:07Z, rc=0). Verbs (ok/total): goto 24/150, dig 40/65, place 9/19, climb 0/16, collect 10/10, craft 0. Deaths ZERO in run. Budget 3.153 wc/min; $0.0776. Furnace: NO, fifth day (.dat only {porkchop:29}; region parse zero). Fence: 0 rows, invariant held unforced.","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-15 trace — 572 rows: 268 cycle rows, dig-guard-arm x1, pit-guard x13, floor-escape x2, failover x1, end row; zero death rows","sha":"04779071fda9"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY15-20261109.md — action curve, furnace (both stores), the walker fence's live evidence, the floor's live report","sha":"e498106f0116"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"the floor's day: VERIFY_FEED first-read pass (have 32); LEASE_ISSUE born launch, flipped live on first heartbeat; ASSERT_DAYLIGHT x22 all attempt 1 (the repaired verification's third consecutive full-day proof); end-of-day PARK/REVOKE on driver_heartbeat_lost 92 s after the clean exit — the expected shape, not an incident; COUNT_DEATH x0"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"frame verdict (9 frames): Cody-visible 1/9 + 1 partial; clean-frame FAILED (chunk voids 2/9; teleport-receipt text 2/9 — one frame carries the full chat backlog panel; canopy 3/9). Keeper exonerated by its own log (SUBJECT-KEEP x10, SUBJECT-HOLD x3, STALL x46 — the STALL count is the bowl's signature). Frame hygiene named the programme's longest-lived unowned deficit, open a fifth day"}],"seq":120,"prev_sha256":"da385897ed710ccba3e8290d3300e2113913e0967a11c8567b5e0c47d1d353ef","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":null,"motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D15:008","anchor":{"citizen_day":15,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T09:09:22Z"},"kind":"floor_act","place":"the camera","what":"Close: Cody OFFLINE in the bowl at (61.7,62,-91.3), hp/food 20/20 (driver-state reads), inventory {cooked_porkchop: 29}, save sha 1b6922ba.... Keeper STOP-stopped; original cameraman relaunched pid 1926346, assertion landed 09:09:22Z, refresh ON. Skill uses[] appended (array's fifth entry, days 11-15).","evidence":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY15-20261109.md — Close state + posture","sha":"e498106f0116"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"what day 16 inherits, per the record: a citizen asleep in a bowl of his own digging at home's edge, fed (29 pork), unhurt, four blocks from his table — and the charter change already named: the below-grade guard + wood-chain-first. 'He must never again be below pad level without a pickaxe in his hand.'"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"the transit problem is filed SOLVED by this day (northern line, flees toward home, zero deaths) — day 15 is the proof"}],"seq":121,"prev_sha256":"e98f348961032c3f0f3033f62a40afdcefd4c3a29d47abe564a6ab18a6427cb8","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":"Morning. I'm in the bowl again — but I know the way out now: east edge, one step up. Let's go home.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D16:001","anchor":{"citizen_day":16,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T09:41:54Z"},"kind":"first","place":"the bowl at home's edge","what":"He woke in the bowl (29 porkchops, hp/food 20/20 — driver-state reads) and aimed at the charter's east step at cycle 1: goto 63 67 -91 NOT arrived; he stood at (61.7,63.2,-91.3), 3.8 below target. The census step exists as a COLUMN; as a STEP it needs a stance at feet 66 — none exists on the pocket floor (feet 61-62).","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-16 trace cycle 1 (09:41:54Z) — goto NOT arrived; he stands at feet 63.2 mid-face, 3.8 below target","sha":"74b127dbf2bf"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY16-20261109.md §2 — the bowl exit: mechanism and cycles (the east step failed geometrically)","sha":"57a2557275a9"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"Gate B was the sequence's first launch with NO refuse-start: claim first (line 355) -> relay RELAY-OK at check and launch (found DOWN — its ELEVENTH death, both VM supervisors dead, no systemd units; relaunched via setsid) -> saves byte-identical (Cody sha 1b6922ba... == day-15 close) -> baseline 136 re-derived (135 + the seam) -> batteries vs shipped md5 9f87c876... (safety 40/40, below-grade 20/20, walker fence 18/18, dig-guard 28/28) -> keeper changeover BEFORE spawn -> floor open -> driver start gate printed the line at 09:41:21Z"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"the charter's census read conflated 'a column whose top is 66' with 'a +1 step from the floor' — the floor is at 60-61, not 65; H1 carries the fault (harness + charter)"}],"seq":122,"prev_sha256":"6f302868e10278548b16ce071d693d64ee87cf9e532bea684c2d8a45054bdf41","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":"The guard reads my target's height, not my feet. So I'll aim at the pad's own level, 67, but pick the nearest column that actually tops at 67 — the grass just west of me. Short leg, pad height, no refusal.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":"harness","thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D16:002","anchor":{"citizen_day":16,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T09:41:58Z"},"kind":"crew_fault","place":"the bowl at home's edge","what":"H1 (HEAD): below-grade guard worked as filed — fixture 20/20, 69 refusals (50 goto, 19 dig), ZERO descent (floor cell byte-identical). But the bound is absolute to the pad and Cody WOKE below it: goto refusals hit mid-level targets (feet 62-65), the only stair cells. Built against ENTRY, it locked a RESIDENT in.","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-16 trace — below-grade-guard rows x69 (first: 09:41:58.132Z, dig (61,63,-90) refused dig-below-pad, padTop 66); cycle 38's say diagnoses the guard's logic in his own words","sha":"74b127dbf2bf"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY16-20261109.md — Incidents H1 (HEAD) + §5 the guards' live accounts","sha":"57a2557275a9"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"the placed rung (charter form 2): ONE placement all day — cycle 48, dirt at (62,65,-89), placed ok — whose top (66) stands +5 over his feet (61): the day-15 error repeated verbatim, a tread too high to step onto. Block 3's 15 place attempts found exactly one landing, at the wrong height; placing a rung AT his level needed a supporting face the pocket's geometry did not give"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"the citizen drew no fault (record's own summary): he diagnosed the guard's logic correctly in his own words by ~cycle 38 ('The guard reads the Y I name, not my feet' — c20; the c38 form is the narration above) and attempted every mechanism the house has ever proven. Standing form (parent note, filed with this seal): a guard bound to the world's constants cannot serve a citizen who wakes outside them — bounds must be relative to the citizen's verified state, or the guard becomes the trap"}],"seq":123,"prev_sha256":"a14a092f7fe1f0a521b0baec5bc7409fe3dd70a1ebd183ac0e35c5d55cf2b528","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":"The digs keep getting cut short. My hands won't finish a swing while something's on me. The skeleton's the real danger at range — but I can't fight a skeleton bare-handed. Let me just try the dig once more; if it aborts again, the wall truly won't give and I'll walk out the south passage instead.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":"world","thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D16:003","anchor":{"citizen_day":16,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T10:25:23Z"},"kind":"near_miss","place":"the bowl at home's edge","what":"H2: the bowl is a gloom cell — creepers/skeletons spawned at the canopy rim under held daylight. From ~10:12Z, 89 flees fired; hop-chains target pad-level points and cannot climb either (moved 0.00-0.97), burning the back half, aborting >=3 digs mid-swing. NO damage: hp 20 in every cycle row (driver-state read).","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-16 trace — floor-escape rows x89 (density blocks 4-8: flee 7/30/21/12/17); cycle 184's say is the mid-swing abort in his own words","sha":"74b127dbf2bf"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY16-20261109.md — Incidents H2 + §5 reflex layer account (end-row floor tally {flee: 89, shelter: 0, eat: 0, forage: 0})","sha":"57a2557275a9"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"the charter priced weather but not gloom-at-home — the day-13/14 rain-gloom lesson recurring in a new place: the bowl and its canopy are a gloom pocket (the census's own tops grid shows canopy over the whole home approach), and gloom spawns at noon"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"pit-guard: 8 refusals, all under flee pressure in the back half — the fallback brain and the flee logic both kept proposing the pit route and the guard kept refusing it; plausibly death-preventing, as day 15 read its 13. Burrow never engaged — the repair gap stands a FOURTH day, not rounded up"}],"seq":124,"prev_sha256":"3a51f1674b74c77def08db481d2eec39e172b704fbc10e60cbf8050586e089eb","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":"Same leg, same result — up to 62 then slid back. The south passage gains me a level but won't hold it. I've retried this twice; the walker won't take me out. Time to stop grinding the same wall and think like a homesteader: the east column tops read lower than south. Let me try a long leg EAST past the water, toward open ground, and see if that face is a real passage.","motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":null,"thread":"furnace","status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D16:004","anchor":{"citizen_day":16,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T11:06:26Z"},"kind":"day_shape","place":"the bowl at home's edge","what":"Day shape: 328 commands across 237 cycles, 85 min (09:41-11:06Z, rc=0). Verbs: goto 139, dig 52, place 17, climb 8, felltree 1, collect 2, CRAFT 0 — wood chain never began; wood-chain-verified row never fired. Deaths ZERO (136->136, three ways). Budget 2.788 wc/min; $0.0839. Furnace: NO, sixth day.","evidence":[{"src":"trace","ref":"day-16 trace — 660 rows: 237 cycle rows, below-grade-guard x69, pit-guard x8, floor-escape x89, failover x1, end row deathsWorld 136; zero death rows","sha":"74b127dbf2bf"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY16-20261109.md — action curve, §1 deaths, §3 the wood chain that never fired, §4 furnace (both stores)","sha":"57a2557275a9"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"the guards' other accounts: dig-guard ZERO live rows a third day — never armed, now structural (its arming path runs through a permitted stone dig, and the below-grade guard stands in front of it; it can only arm on days he already holds a pickaxe). Walker fence 0 rows — the I4 invariant held a third day, unfired. Safety reading path: no park, no abort, no gate event all day — correct (no death occurred; the lease never faulted)"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"the floor's day: VERIFY_FEED PASS first-read (need 8, have 29); LEASE_ISSUE 09:41:06Z born launch; ASSERT_DAYLIGHT x22, every 240 s, attempt-1 landings verified against the verbatim mirror (last 11:05:11Z); no park, no revoke, no alert all day. The skill's seventh uses[] entry appended (the array now holds 6 entries — days 11-16)"}],"seq":125,"prev_sha256":"aaf5c13acbc0b6428fab12e2511316159adc25a82846545a9cc67d0c0f7e7488","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
{"subject":"cody","narration":null,"motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":"harness","thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D16:005","anchor":{"citizen_day":16,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T10:12:00Z"},"kind":"floor_act","place":"the home district","what":"Weather act (§6): /weather clear issued by Gallery 09:40:24Z, verified landed issuer-specifically — and rain appears in 2 of 6 sampled frames inside the window. A momentary clear is not a hold; the act as chartered does not hold weather, filed as insufficient. Day 17 made weather a floor-class HOLD (b:D17:005).","evidence":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY16-20261109.md §6 — frame verdict's weather read ('RAIN. Two of the six frames...') + §8 Gate B (the act, issued and verified landed)","sha":"57a2557275a9"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"frame verdict over 6 frames (G1, lane, minor: the charter's >=9 was not met — capture retention pruned two target epochs and sampling ran after close; counts are reported over 6 and say so): Cody visible 2/6 fully; chunk voids 1/6; canopy 2/6; surface-without-him 2/6 (aim, not hygiene)"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"the hygiene finding: receipt text 0/6 and full chat panel 0/6 — day 15's defects did NOT recur, with NO client change made (chatVisibility:1 untouched, clean-frame toggle OFF). Day 15's panel frame now reads as a transient client UI state, not a standing defect. Keeper's log: SUBJECT-KEEP x2, SUBJECT-HOLD x22, STALL x49 — it held its last frame because he never moved >3 blocks in open view; the bowl hid the citizen"}],"seq":126,"prev_sha256":"c2023132120fdf7ef1d4b53060dcb0e1a86fd22dbf21693d16414eaa1dd4a095","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
