{"subject":"cody","narration":null,"motive_ref":null,"fault_owner":"harness","thread":null,"status":"sealed","supersedes":null,"corrects":null,"observations_gap":null,"id":"b:D17:002","anchor":{"citizen_day":17,"wall_utc":"2026-11-10T12:00:00Z"},"kind":"crew_fault","place":"the scratch rig","what":"Arm A (place-ladder north): 0/3. Rung 1 gained 3/3 — dig wall's foot cell (61,62,-90), place dug block, step on: server feet 63. Rung 2 refused 3/3: next place reports target already stone — rung-1 block stands in the only reachable cell; face above is the wall's own stone. One-rung law, reproduced in the bowl.","evidence":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"DIRECT-DRIVE-DAY17-20261109.md §2 — the rehearsal curve (arm A) + the replica verification discipline","sha":"d98e1e52df8c"}],"observations":[{"src":"day_record","ref":"the replica's probe is itself filed: data get block returns NBT only for block entities on this build, so verification ran execute-if-blocks type-equality against reference cells — validated against known cells before use, and its one blind spot (a dirt cell matches a grass_block reference under masked comparison) was found and fixed by probing grass_block FIRST"},{"src":"day_record","ref":"Incident R1 (rig): the replica build's grass caps reverted to dirt across six verification aborts (a grass cell covered by leaf litter inside the build's own clear volume) — each abort was the cell-by-cell verify doing its job; fixed by per-cell cap forcing. The verify gate never let an unverified replica run an arm. Rehearsal 1's earlier 0/3s (an invalid, overlapping-fill replica) are filed as artefacts, not evidence"}],"seq":129,"prev_sha256":"73702799c0cc03a400ebd64de95ed80b33eb8da22f99a99ed40860319c35dfdf","written_utc":"2026-11-10T15:27:02.098Z","writer":{"process":"chronicle-seal-11-17","version":"1.0.0"}}
